-- A named site and a construction that leave out a TYPICALLY default which is an
-- EXPRESSION (TYPICALLY-ONE-BEHAVIOUR-SPEC.md W7). The checker copies the
-- expression to the site, with every token and range of the declaration it was
-- written in cleared; the Check phase below must still have tokens for this
-- file, and none at the site for what the default names.

GIVETH A NUMBER
phi MEANS 8

GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (phi PLUS 1)
      base IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
scaled MEANS rate TIMES base

DECLARE Paint
  HAS coats IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (phi TIMES 2)
      gloss IS A NUMBER

GIVETH A NUMBER
`one` MEANS scaled WITH base IS 1

GIVETH A Paint
`two` MEANS Paint WITH gloss IS 2

#EVAL `one`
